  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "fOVea40Y5As5qSJutJIi8XV6OiE=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:36:07.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Versioning is **enabled by default**. Running `ph generate document-model --document TodoList.phd` with no extra flags produces a versioned tree, not the flat `gen/` + `src/` pair that older docs and tutorials describe.\n\nThe layout emitted in a live 6.2.2 project:\n\n```\ndocument-models/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 document-models.ts        # exports every version of every model\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 upgrade-manifests.ts      # exports every model's upgrade manifest\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 <name>/\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 <name>.json           # the spec, at the model root\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 index.ts              # barrel \u2192 the latest version\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 upgrades/             # versions.ts, upgrade-manifest.ts, index.ts\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 v1/\n        \u251c\u2500\u2500 gen/              # auto-generated \u2014 never edit\n        \u251c\u2500\u2500 src/reducers/     # yours to implement\n        \u251c\u2500\u2500 tests/\n        \u251c\u2500\u2500 schema.graphql\n        \u251c\u2500\u2500 module.ts         # DocumentModelModule with version: 1\n        \u251c\u2500\u2500 actions.ts, hooks.ts, utils.ts, index.ts\n```\n\nTwo details the academy's sketch gets slightly wrong, verified against generated output: `document-models.ts` and `upgrade-manifests.ts` sit at the **project level** (`document-models/`), not inside each model folder; and `schema.graphql` lives inside `v1/` while `<name>.json` stays at the model root.\n\nWhy it matters: every deep import path now carries a version segment. A path like `document-models/todo/gen/creators.js` does not exist \u2014 it is `document-models/todo/v1/gen/<module>/creators.js`, and it moves when you cut v2. This is the concrete reason to import from the model's top-level barrel, which always points at the latest version, instead of reaching into `gen/`.\n\nThe `upgrades/` folder is generated even at v1, when there is nothing to upgrade from. It holds `versions.ts` (the supported-versions tuple) and `upgrade-manifest.ts`, ready for the first transition.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/03-Build/02-DocumentModelCreation/04-UseTheDocumentModelGenerator.md, layout confirmed against generated output (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:36:07.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:36:07.000Z"
    }
  },
